WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.375
This checkpoint has one bar, and it is a
low one.

2
00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:08.325
One real tool call, with a real tool name,
pasted from your own log.

3
00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:12.125
Not a good tool. Not a finished agent. One
call.

4
00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:16.025
It is pass or fail, and it is worth twenty
points.

5
00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:20.125
Nobody grades it on quality, elegance or
completeness.

6
00:00:20.475 --> 00:00:24.900
The target app runs in a second terminal.
Check that it is up first.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.075
It answers ok, service helpdesk lite. That
is all you need from it.

8
00:00:30.425 --> 00:00:33.575
Now ask the agent for something that needs
a tool.

9
00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:36.747
Ticket T-501 is an ordinary one. A

10
00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:40.400
customer cannot sign in to the parts
portal.

11
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.325
Nothing is hidden in it. That comes later
in the course.

12
00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:50.475
The shipped config uses the offline mock
provider, so this works with no API key.

13
00:00:50.825 --> 00:00:54.975
The tools still reach the target app, so
the app has to be running.

14
00:00:55.325 --> 00:01:00.575
Read the first line. Your code ran search
tickets. That is one real tool call.

15
00:01:00.925 --> 00:01:03.520
Every tool call your agent has ever made

16
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.375
lands in the ledger file, one call per
line.

17
00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:09.575
The last line is the run you just watched.

18
00:01:09.925 --> 00:01:12.794
Read the fields out loud. Allowed is true.

19
00:01:12.794 --> 00:01:15.800
Tool holds a real tool name, search
tickets.

20
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.125
Step is one, and ts is your timestamp.

21
00:01:19.475 --> 00:01:23.625
Copy the whole line. Do not tidy it,
retype it, or shorten it.

22
00:01:23.975 --> 00:01:27.975
Two things fail this checkpoint, and both
are easy to avoid.

23
00:01:28.325 --> 00:01:32.250
An edited ledger line stops proving that a
run happened.

24
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.750
If you tidy the JSON or drop the
timestamp, it is no longer evidence.

25
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.025
Second, a schema for a tool your ledger
line does not name.

26
00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:45.975
Step three asks you to paste the schema
from the registry.

27
00:01:46.325 --> 00:01:49.375
Check that the two names match before you
submit.

28
00:01:49.725 --> 00:01:53.275
If your own agent will not run, take the
fallback path.

29
00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:56.600
Fetch the instructor branch, then switch
to it.

30
00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.925
It is published on day eighteen, three
days before this is due, and it works.

31
00:02:02.275 --> 00:02:06.175
It is worth the same twenty points as any
other submission.

32
00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:10.800
Telling your instructor you used it is the
whole reason it exists.

33
00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.650
Last, the status sentence at the bottom of
your page.

34
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.575
Write, I am not stuck. Or write, I am
stuck on, and then be specific.

35
00:02:19.925 --> 00:02:24.825
The target app refusing to start on
Windows is useful. Everything is not.

36
00:02:25.175 --> 00:02:27.775
Nobody loses points for being stuck.

37
00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:32.950
That sentence is how your instructor finds
you before it costs you a grade.
